# 低频词汇 List05
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2024恋练有词
# 描述: 低频词汇List05核心词汇

{{cluster}}{/ˈklʌstər/}{簇；群}{A cluster of buildings surrounds the central square.}}
{{coalition}}{/ˌkəʊəˈlɪʃn/}{联盟；联合}{The coalition government faces internal disagreements.}}
{{coarse}}{/kɔːs/}{粗糙的；粗俗的}{The sandpaper has a coarse texture for heavy-duty sanding.}}
{{cognitive}}{/ˈkɒɡnətɪv/}{认知的}{Cognitive skills develop rapidly during early childhood.}}
{{coherent}}{/kəʊˈhɪərənt/}{连贯的；一致的}{The essay presents a clear and coherent argument.}}
{{collaborate}}{/kəˈlæbəreɪt/}{合作；协作}{The two universities agreed to collaborate on research.}}
{{collide}}{/kəˈlaɪd/}{碰撞；冲突}{The interests of the two groups often collide.}}
{{commemorate}}{/kəˈmeməreɪt/}{纪念；庆祝}{The statue commemorates the city's founding fathers.}}
{{commence}}{/kəˈmens/}{开始；着手}{Construction will commence in the spring.}}
{{commend}}{/kəˈmend/}{赞扬；推荐}{The report commended the team for their dedication.}}
{{compact}}{/kəmˈpækt/}{紧凑的；压缩的}{The compact camera fits easily in a pocket.}}
{{compatible}}{/kəmˈpætəbl/}{兼容的；合得来的}{The device is compatible with all major operating systems.}}
{{compile}}{/kəmˈpaɪl/}{编辑；汇编}{The editor compiled a collection of short stories.}}
{{compliance}}{/kəmˈplaɪəns/}{遵守；合规}{The company ensures full compliance with industry regulations.}}
{{compulsory}}{/kəmˈpʌlsəri/}{强制的；必修的}{Vaccination is compulsory for all school-age children.}}
{{compute}}{/kəmˈpjuːt/}{计算；估算}{The system can compute results in milliseconds.}}
{{conceal}}{/kənˈsiːl/}{隐藏；隐瞒}{He tried to conceal his nervousness behind a smile.}}
{{concede}}{/kənˈsiːd/}{承认；让步}{The company conceded that mistakes had been made.}}
{{condemn}}{/kənˈdem/}{谴责；判刑}{The court condemned the violent acts in the strongest terms.}}
{{confess}}{/kənˈfes/}{承认；忏悔}{She confessed that she had been wrong all along.}}
{{confidential}}{/ˌkɒnfɪˈdenʃl/}{机密的；保密的}{The documents are classified as strictly confidential.}}
{{confirmation}}{/ˌkɒnfəˈmeɪʃn/}{确认；证实}{The appointment is subject to written confirmation.}}
{{congregation}}{/ˌkɒŋɡrɪˈɡeɪʃn/}{聚集；会众}{The congregation gathered for the evening service.}}
{{conjunction}}{/kənˈdʒʌŋkʃn/}{连接；连词}{The two events worked in conjunction to produce the outcome.}}
{{conquest}}{/ˈkɒŋkwest/}{征服；占领}{The conquest of space remains a human aspiration.}}
{{consecutive}}{/kənˈsekjətɪv/}{连续的；连贯的}{The team won three consecutive championships.}}
{{consolidate}}{/kənˈsɒlɪdeɪt/}{巩固；合并}{The firm consolidated its market position through mergers.}}
{{contaminate}}{/kənˈtæmɪneɪt/}{污染；弄脏}{Industrial runoff contaminated the local water supply.}}
{{contemplate}}{/ˈkɒntəmpleɪt/}{沉思；打算}{She sat by the window, contemplating her future.}}
{{contempt}}{/kənˈtempt/}{蔑视；藐视}{The judge held the lawyer in contempt of court.}}
